Hi,

I've long lamented the relative lack of distinction between carrying,
wielding and wearing the Amulet of Yendor. Shouldn't there be some
extra-special effect for putting such a mighty Artifact around your
neck? I propose that instead of merely getting warm near portals, it
activates Hard Mode, in which:

* If you are not fire resistant, you die.
  ("The Amulet tightens around your neck and sears a firey channel
through your flesh as it drops to the floor.")
* The Amulet auto-curses and cannot be uncursed or removed in any way.
  ("The amulet tightens around your neck, as you realise you will carry
it to your grave or glory!")
  This only works in the Sanctum - putting it on elsewhere gives the
traditional effect.
* Your wisdom is abused.
* You gain 5 charisma points.
* All the usual amulet-carrying effects are in place (mysterious force,
etc.)
* You lose 1 MaxHP every 100 turns.
* You lose all but d10 of your divine protection.
* The summon nasties spell has a 1 in 13 chance of summoning Demogorgon
directly.
* The Wizard reincarnates twice as often.
* Three times the usual number of randomly generated monsters are
generated, except on the planes.
* Whenever you go up a staircase, there is a 1 in 13 chance of your
MaxPW being decreased by 10 points, but gaining the confuse monster
effect for d50 (more) turns.
  ("You lose control of your magical energy!")
  If the d10 decrease would set your MaxPW to below zero, your hunger
status is set to Weak, and you are stunned for d50 (more) turns.
  ("You feel the Amulet taking a terrible toll on your mind and body.")
* Your end of game attributes say "You were a hero/heroine".

Some comments:

* This means you can't use an amulet of life saving.
* The instadeath can occur whenever you lose fire resistance, so watch
out for gremlins!
* A new fortune may be required: "They say the Amulet of Yendor is worn
by the mighty and the foolish."

I hope I've not included anything that would require a major revision
of the source code, because I'm really hoping for some keen patchmakers
to step up to the challenge and... well, do all the work for me :)

Any comments?

